{
  // Declaration-only build. The lib is plain JS + JSX; this exists purely to
  // emit .d.ts so consumers stop hand-maintaining their own copy of the API.
  //
  // Before this, package.json pointed `types` at dist/index.d.ts — a file
  // nothing ever produced. Every TypeScript consumer therefore wrote its own
  // `declare module '@omni-design/components'` shim and it drifted behind the
  // lib silently: the studio's was missing eleven components that had been
  // shipping for months, and nothing failed until someone imported one.
  //
  // Types are INFERRED from the source (prop destructuring + defaults), so a
  // component gains real prop types without annotating anything, and a
  // component added to src/components/index.js appears here automatically.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false,
    "declaration": true,
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true,
    // The dependency tree ships .d.ts using syntax older compilers cannot
    // PARSE (skipLibCheck skips checking, not parsing), so this needs TS >= 5.
    //
    // build:types runs it via `npx -p typescript@5.9` rather than depending on
    // a local install. react-scripts pins typescript to ^3.2.1 || ^4 as a peer,
    // so adding 5.9 as a devDependency makes npm re-resolve the whole tree and
    // emit a wall of peerOptional WARNINGS — which read as failure, and take
    // long enough with no output that the install gets interrupted.
    //
    // Pinned, not floating: the declarations are a published artefact, and a
    // compiler drifting under them would change output with no commit.
    // Cached, this runs in ~2s.
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "jsx": "react",
    "target": "ES2020",
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "node",
    "rootDir": "src",
    "outDir": "dist/types",
    "noEmitOnError": false
  },
  "include": ["src/components/index.js", "src/OmniDesignProvider.js"]
}
